%N A401818 Side lengths of squares formed by constructing three right triangles corresponding to distinct Pythagorean triples on the sides of a triangle excluding configurations that are integer multiples of previously obtained configurations.
%C A401818 A possible ordered 6-tuple solution (p,x,y,a,b,c) satisfying the simultaneous equations: p^2 + x^2 = a^2, (p-x)^2 + y^2 = b^2, (p-y)^2 + p^2 = c^2 represent three distinct Pythagorean triples (p,x,a), (p-x,y,b), (p,p-y,c) corresponding to the right-angled triangles formed on the sides of the triangle with integer side lengths a, b and c. The sequence is generated by the primitive integer solutions for p.
%C A401818 A401818 is a subsequence of A400178.
%H A401818 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A401818/a401818_1.txt">Python Code for A401818</a>
%e A401818 First valid ordered 6-tuple solution (360,105,136,375,289,424) represents the three distinct Pythagorean triples (360,105,375), (255,136,289), (360,224,424) corresponding to the right-angled triangles constructed on the sides of the triangle of side lengths 375, 289 and 424. Therefore, the first term of the sequence is 360.
%Y A401818 Cf. A400178, A046083, A046084, A009000.
